<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia produces 1.39 mln bpd crude oil in May.</title>
<headline>Indonesia produces 1.39 mln bpd crude oil in May.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia produced around 1.39 million barrels per day of crude oil in May and about 170,000 bpd of condensate, oil industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Indonesia produced 1.56 million bpd of crude oil and condensate in May. It produced about 1.39 million of crude oil and the rest is condensate,&quot; one source said.</p>
<p>The sources said some 60,000 bpd of crude was used for a steamflood project in the Duri field in Central Sumatra.</p>
<p>The Duri field produces around 280,000 bpd of crude, operated by Caltex Pacific Indonesia, jointly owned by Chevron Corp and Texaco.</p>
</text>
